    {
      "id": "lifecycle",
      "title": "Lifecycle",
      "deck": "Cold start after the OS file cache was purged: from the launch command to the frontend's first animation frame, on one wall clock, 20 launches each. Warm start immediately after a prior launch, 10 each. Then a 10-minute soak cycling the three parity tests with a 1 MB round trip every 5 s, footprint sampled every second, 3 soaks each.",
      "unit": "ms",
      "lowerIsBetter": true,
      "verdict": {
        "winnerId": "electron",
        "headline": "Cold start is a tie at about 1.1 s with the file cache purged; over ten minutes of work Electron averaged 349 MB to Tauri's 561",
        "summary": "Warm starts tie too, at about 305 ms. Memory is where the Mac surprised me: the number is physical footprint over every process the app is responsible for, which is the only way to count WKWebView's helpers at all (a plain process-tree sum misses them entirely). Counted that way, Tauri's content process climbed past 1 GB in two of three soaks and hit 2.4 GB once, each time at the end of a table segment, and came back down. Electron's renderer never passed 365 MB. Footprint swings with the segment in both shells, roughly a third as much during the table as during the particles, so the mean over the soak is the figure to quote, not the last sample."
      },
